meta {
  name: List Outgoing Requests
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/com.community.graph.listFollowRequests?direction=outgoing&status=pending&limit=50
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

params:query {
  direction: outgoing
  status: pending
  limit: 50
}

docs {
  # List Outgoing Requests
  
  Lists follow requests that you have sent to other users (your requests to follow private profiles).
  
  ## Query Parameters
  - `direction` (string): "outgoing" - requests you sent to others
  - `status` (string, optional): Filter by status ("pending", "approved", "denied")
  - `limit` (number, optional): Maximum number of results (default: 50)
  - `cursor` (string, optional): Pagination cursor
  
  ## Response
  Returns a list of your follow requests:
  ```json
  {
    "requests": [
      {
        "uri": "at://did:plc:your-did/com.community.graph.followRequest/xxx",
        "cid": "...",
        "value": {
          "subject": "did:plc:alice-did",
          "status": "pending",
          "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
        },
        "subject": {
          "did": "did:plc:alice-did",
          "handle": "alice.example.com",
          "displayName": "Alice"
        }
      }
    ],
    "cursor": "..."
  }
  ```
  
  ## Test Scenario
  Used to check status of sent requests:
  1. Bob authenticates
  2. Bob sends follow request to Alice (private profile)
  3. Bob lists outgoing requests
  4. Verify request to Alice appears with status "pending"
  5. Bob can track when Alice approves/denies the request
  
  **Common Use Case:** Show a list of pending outgoing requests in the UI so the user can track their status.
}
